# v0.3 — funnel step layout (canonical)

## Stack (required for new / edited funnel steps)

```tsx
<FunnelStepRoot fitViewport aria-label="…">
  {/* bleed / heroes — absolute, not in flex flow */}
  <FunnelStepBackground>…</FunnelStepBackground>
  {/* or existing absolute backdrop components */}

  <FunnelStepForeground distribution="between" fitViewport>
    <FunnelStepSection>…hero / copy…</FunnelStepSection>
    <FunnelStepMain>{/* scroll here if needed */}</FunnelStepMain>
    <FunnelStepFooter primaryLabel="…" onPrimary={…} />
  </FunnelStepForeground>
</FunnelStepRoot>
```

Primitives: `src/components/ui/funnel-layout/*`. Spacing helpers: `src/constants/funnel-vertical-layout.ts`.

Auth/help screens may use `AuthFunnelScreenShell` (same stack underneath) — do not invent a third shell.

## Rules

1. **`fitViewport`** on `FunnelStepRoot` + `FunnelStepForeground` for full-screen funnel steps so short phones shrink the canvas to usable height instead of outer page scroll.
2. **Background bleed** stays absolute / out of flex (`FunnelStepBackground` or existing backdrop). Do not put full-bleed heroes inside `FunnelStepMain` flex flow.
3. **CTAs** go in `FunnelStepFooter` (or shared blur-footer constants). Do **not** add new absolute-positioned footer/CTA components.
4. **Scroll** lives in `FunnelStepMain` when content overflows — not a new page-level scroll wrapper.
5. **Gutters:** `px-v03-gutter` / `w-v03-content` — no extra horizontal margin.
6. **No** per-component `transform: scale()` to “fit” short screens — fix at `FunnelViewport` / this stack.

## Out of scope

| Surface | Layout |
|---------|--------|
| `/` landing | Responsive marketing — not 375×812 funnel |
| `/dashboard/*` | `100dvh` dashboard chrome (S4) — not `FunnelStepRoot` |
| `/child/*` token URLs | Legacy v0.2 until explicitly migrated |

## Anti-patterns

- New `Onboarding*Cta` / absolute footer shells parallel to `FunnelStepFooter`
- Hardcoding `height: 812` on step roots when `fitViewport` should drive height
- Migrating dashboard cards into the funnel artboard stack
